From: lukasloetkolben <61192133+lukasloetkolben@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 11 Apr 2026 11:43:55 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] xnor-tech: Tesla Model S legacy CAN ignition detection

Add Tesla Model S (legacy, pre-Raven) ignition detection via GTW_status
(0x348). Ignition tracks msg->data[0] bit 0, gated on the GTW rolling
counter (data[6] low nibble) to reject bus noise.

Upstream moved ignition_can_hook() from panda into
opendbc/safety/ignition.h (#2396); the Model S legacy hook lives here
now. VW MEB detection (also previously carried in the panda patch) is
already upstream in this file, so it is no longer carried by the fork.
---
 opendbc/safety/ignition.h | 13 +++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+)

diff --git a/opendbc/safety/ignition.h b/opendbc/safety/ignition.h
index ae00c729..c8ff3fb6 100644
--- a/opendbc/safety/ignition.h
+++ b/opendbc/safety/ignition.h
@@ -68,6 +68,19 @@ void ignition_can_hook(const CANPacket_t *msg) {
     }
   }
 
+  // Tesla Model S (legacy) exception
+  if (((msg->bus == 0U) || (msg->bus == 1U)) && (msg->addr == 0x348U) && (GET_LEN(msg) == 8)) {
+    int counter = msg->data[6] & 0xFU;
+
+    static int prev_counter_tesla_legacy = -1;
+    if ((counter == ((prev_counter_tesla_legacy + 1) % 16)) && (prev_counter_tesla_legacy != -1)) {
+      // GTW_status
+      ignition_can = (msg->data[0] & 0x1U) != 0U;
+      ignition_can_cnt = 0U;
+    }
+    prev_counter_tesla_legacy = counter;
+  }
+
   // TODO: this is too loose, Teslas have 0x222
   // body v2 exception
   // if (((msg->bus == 0U) || (msg->bus == 2U)) && (msg->addr == 0x222U)) {
